<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine MerVal index adds two new stocks.</title>
<headline>Argentine MerVal index adds two new stocks.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's weighted MerVal stock index added two stocks in its quarterly revision based on trading volume, the Buenos Aires bolsa said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The stocks added were holding company Cresud and cement firm Corcemar, taking the total amount of stocks on the roster to 27, as follows:</p>
<p>Acindar</p>
<p>Alpargatas</p>
<p>Astra</p>
<p>Banco Frances</p>
<p>Banco Galicia</p>
<p>Bansud</p>
<p>Celulosa</p>
<p>Central Costanera</p>
<p>Central Puerto</p>
<p>Ciadea</p>
<p>Comercial del Plata</p>
<p>Corcemar</p>
<p>Cresud</p>
<p>Garovaglio</p>
<p>Indupa</p>
<p>IRSA</p>
<p>Juan Minetti</p>
<p>Molinos Rio de la Plata</p>
<p>Telecom</p>
<p>Telefonica</p>
<p>Transportadora de Gas del Sur</p>
<p>Perez Companc</p>
<p>Polledo</p>
<p>Sevel</p>
<p>Siderar</p>
<p>Siderca</p>
<p>YPF</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom 541 318-0657))</p>
</text>
